From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:32:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: do not force useLLInt back on when wasm cannot run

disableAllWasmJITOptions() turned useLLInt on unconditionally, so a
configuration with the JITs off and wasm off (or a wasm-less build with
--useLLInt=0 for the C loop) had an explicit --useLLInt=0 overridden and
tripped the option coherence check. The LLInt only has to be on as wasm's
fallback engine, so only force it when wasm itself is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
index 683bc60a7a87..757960fa1c4c 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
@@ -697,8 +697,10 @@ void Options::setAllJITCodeValidations(bool value)
 static inline void NODELETE disableAllWasmJITOptions()
 {
 #if ENABLE(WEBASSEMBLY)
-    // This really only makes sense if could use wasm, otherwise we should not override this.
-    Options::useLLInt() = true;
+    // The LLInt is wasm's fallback engine, so keep it on without the wasm JITs, but
+    // only if wasm can run: otherwise this would override an explicit --useLLInt=0.
+    if (Options::useWasm())
+        Options::useLLInt() = true;
 #endif
     Options::useBBQJIT() = false;
     Options::useOMGJIT() = false;
